{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"## Findings\n\n- **P1 — Production multiplexed waiters are missing from the W4-feeding census.** The `dao.stream.serving` row omits acknowledgement-slot polling performed by `ws/endpoint-step` at `src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:565-591`, even though `serving/step!` invokes it at `serving.cljc:339-342`. More importantly, `yin.repl.serve/step` separately multiplexes every adopted session through `advance-sessions`/`session-step` at `serve.cljc:586-619`, including request reads and retained response retries. These are not represented by the serving row and are precisely the production multi-waiter loops W4 must classify.\n\n- **P1 — The “no loop of their own” verification is contradicted by source.** At plan lines 221-225:\n  - `dao.stream.forward/forward-step` contains a bounded polling loop at `forward.cljc:101-140`.\n  - `yin.repl.connect/observe` contains a budgeted polling loop at `connect.cljc:537-556`, not “one `stream/next` per call.”\n\n- **P2 — Additional census omissions weaken the claim of completeness.** Examples include the single-medium FFI bridge loop in `yin/vm/ffi.cljc:237-244` and the one-shot `dao.space.index/snapshot-datoms` drain at `index.cljc:445-452`. These likely remain unchanged, but the census explicitly includes comparable single-stream and one-shot drains, so their absence is inconsistent.\n\nRequired spot checks:\n\n- The `yin.vm.engine` row is faithful: resolution, reader/writer polling, ordered sweep, shared-cursor write-back, and `run-loop` integration match `engine.cljc:266-368` and `:374-388`.\n- The named `dao.stream.serving` functions at `serving.cljc:260-351` are described correctly, but the row is incomplete because it excludes the endpoint acknowledgement sweep invoked inside the same tick.\n- The JVM, Node, and Dart REPL cadence owners at `repl.cljc:194`, `:267`, and `:352` are accurately cited. The aggregate description of what their tick polls is incomplete because it obscures the additional lifecycle and per-session loops beneath `serve/step`.\n\nScope is correct: within the target file, the diff changes only the introductory status/date line and adds the W0 census under Phase W0. No files were edited during this review.\n\nSIGN-OFF: denied — The W0 census omits production multiplexed acknowledgement and REPL-session polling loops and contains source-contradicted no-loop claims, so it cannot safely determine W4 adoption."}}
